module

public import ReasLib.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace.EtaleSite.Spaces
import StacksCheckRecall

@[expose] public section

universe u

/- Definition 66.18.2: let `S` be a scheme and let `X` be an algebraic space over `S`.
The site `X_spaces,étale` of `X` is the Grothendieck topology `spacesEtaleTopology X` on
the category `spacesEtaleSite X` of algebraic spaces étale over `X` (objects are étale
morphisms `φ : U ⟶ X` of algebraic spaces over `S` with `Etale φ`, morphisms
`χ : U ⟶ U'` over `X` satisfy `χ ≫ φ' = φ`). The precoverage
`spacesEtalePrecoverage X` consists of presieves presented by `Type u`-indexed
families jointly surjective on points, expressed as
`⋃ i, Set.range (Points.map (χ i).left) = Set.univ`.
The topology `spacesEtaleTopology X` is generated by this precoverage. The fixed
universe supplies the ambient size convention. The scheme-chart inclusion
`smallEtaleInclusion X` has domain `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace.SmallEtale.site X`,
whose covering families are included among these jointly surjective families. -/
@[stacks 03G0] #check (AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace.spacesEtaleTopology :
  ∀ {S : AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.{u}} (X : AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace S),
    CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology (AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace.spacesEtaleSite X))
